# Context7

Use the Context7 MCP (`user-context7`) whenever you need documentation for a library, framework, SDK, API, CLI, or cloud service — including well-known ones like Next.js, React, Tailwind, and shadcn. Prefer it over web search and over training memory.

Do not use Context7 for refactors, writing scripts from scratch, debugging business logic, code review, or general programming concepts.

## How to look up docs

1. Call `resolve-library-id` with the official library name and a specific query.
2. Call `query-docs` with the returned Context7 library ID (format `/org/project`) and one focused topic per call.
3. Do not call either tool more than 3 times per question.

For Next.js App Router APIs in this repo, also read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — this version has breaking changes that Context7 may not match.
